  "body": "Part of #290; rides #535 (wire op pages). Found while building #537.\n\n**What happens now.** #537's 4-axis block is edited on the Wire Contour page as numbers: the pairing rule, the twist tolerance, and each sync pair's upper and lower point as X/Y fields. The two profiles are the op's ordinary selection (two faces or closed chains at two heights).\n\n**Wanted.** Pick a sync pair in the viewport: click a vertex of the upper profile, then one of the lower (an unpaired half is already storable - `WireSyncPair { upper, lower: None }` - and refused by name at generation), with the stored pairs drawn as rulings over the model. The page should also say which pick is read as the upper profile and which as the lower.\n\nEvidence: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wire_page.rs` (`four_axis_fields`), `crates/app/src/operation/types/wire_edm.rs` (`WireFourAxis`).\n\n**Done means:** a sync pair is created by two vertex clicks through `EditOperationParams` (undoable), the pairs are drawn, and the structural UI test asserts the rows and the pick state; no snapshot PNG changes.\n",
